From u870152baa62da8c4 at groups.google.com  Wed Sep  1 20:29:57 2010
From: u870152baa62da8c4 at groups.google.com (Erik Benton)
Date: Wed, 01 Sep 2010 20:29:57 +0000
Subject: RHEL/Centos 64bit compile hint
Message-ID: <ocrE2niXJ7E.abev1IvQYj4J@rapache.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rapache/c/ocrE2niXJ7E/m/abev1IvQYj4J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I just wanted to let folks know that there is a problem with libapreq2
that comes bundled with the rapache module source. By default it
assumes a /usr/lib directory on the ld path. If you happen to be
running a 64bit OS your libs are probably under /usr/lib64 instead.
Before running ./configure you can execute the following to add the
correct lib path to ld:

LDFLAGS=-L/usr/lib64

This bit me for a little bit while I traced why it was attempting to
use the 32bit libs.

-Erik

